      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-02-10_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <head>MARMALADE</head>
        <p>MARMALADE</p>
        <p>is absolutely pure</p>
        <p>New Season's now ready</p>
        <p>ITRE WARRINGTON MUSEUM COMMITTEE beg to announce that the following Popular •4enturea Will be delivered under the auspices of the Ogden Trustees. SATURDAY, FEBRUAhY 10TH, "The Treasures of Rome," BY C. ROWLEY, ESQ. CHAIRMAN : THOMAS BIRTLES, ESQ. 44 Pr, SATURDAY, FEBRUARY 17Th, 'Ltle Pre-raphzelite Brotherhood : Holman Hunt, Millais, Rossetti and others,' BY J. E. PHYTHIAN, ESQ. r_ tATAIRMAN :W.H. J. JENKINS, EQ. 4.-antern Illustrations at the MASONIC HALL, BOLD ST., at 7.90 p.m. Admission Free.</p>
        <p>COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER. DESTRUCTIVE INSECTS AND PESTS Acrs 1877 and 1907.</p>
        <p>THE Cheshire County Council invite applications from suitable persons who have some Knowledge of Farming and Gardening, for the position of INSPECTOR under the above ACTS and the Orders of the Board of Agriculture and Fisheries for the Adminis- trative County of Chester. The person appointed will be required to reside at such place in the County as the County Council may with the approval of the Board of Agriculture and Fisheries determine and to devote the whole of his time to the duties of his office, which will be determined by the Inspector of the Board of Agri- culture and Fisheries for the County under whose supervision he will act. The Salary to be £IS per annum, payable monthly, with an allowance for travelling (Railway) expenses of not exceeding One Penny per mile, with an additional suitable mileage allowance, to be determined by the Council, for use of bioycle,the total travelling expenses not to exceed £4 monthly. The appointment to be for one year, commencing Ist April 1912, and may be determined by the County Council upon One Month's Notice. Applications, stating age and qualifications, accom- paniedby 3 recent testimonials, to be received by the , undersigned not later than the 17th day of February 1912. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk to the County Council. County Offices, Northgate at., Chester.</p>
