      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-02-10_WidnesExaminer_art0106" n="art0106">
        <head>CAN ALWAYS BE CURED BY</head>
        <p>CAN ALWAYS BE CURED BY</p>
        <p>MR. LIWNARD GREEN, The Polygon Cigar Stores, of 38, Stockport Road, Ardwick, Manchester, says : "In December, 1903, I began to suffer from indigestion. Food caused 111`2 fearful pain in my stomach, where it used to remain, a hard immovable mass. There was also a constant feeling of stuffiness, a difficulty in breathing, very uncomfortable to endure. It occurred to me that it would be better for me if I ate as little as possible, so I restricted my diet to such a degree that, for lack of food, I became quite weak ; and that, too, without my power of digestion being much improved. Such was my state of health when I bought my first bottle of Mother Seigel's Syrup. It did me good, almost from the first dose. Three or four bottles of the Syrup proved sufficient .for my lasting cure." April 18, 1910.</p>
