        <p>RUNCORN LIBERALS' FANCY DRESS BALL TORIES ATTRACTED. The Runcorn Liberals had a fancy dress ball o Wednesday night, the first held in the town for a number of years. About 400 assembled in th Drill Hall. Mr. F. J. Norman, the local leader of the party, in a short address expressed his pleasure at seeing so many Conservatives present, and said the spirit shown might clear up many misunderstandings. Mr. J. F. L. Brunner, M.P., also welcomed those present in s felicitous speech. The hall was charmingly decorated, and the costumes of the ladies were very original and pretty. Prizes were given, Mesdames Posnett, Carroll, Lightfoot and Macdonald judging. The results were : Ladies :-1, Miss Bunion, GAlywrig ; 2, Mrs NV Shaw, Bridge; 3, M iss Dutton, Milkmaid. Special prizes: Mrs Stubbs, Home Rule ; Miss Johnson, Indian Lady. Gentlemen Mr G Forrester, Dandy Coon ; 2, Mr W Brimelow, Harem Skirt.</p>
